# Exclusions for the image build.
#
# This file has to live HERE, beside the Dockerfile, not at the repository root. Docker
# reads `<context>/.dockerignore`, and the build context is environment/ -- Harbor sets it
# that way and docker-compose.yml matches. The root .dockerignore is never consulted for
# this build, which is why its `*.md` rule needed an exception for data/README.md that could
# never have applied.
#
# Paths are relative to environment/.

# Python build residue that must never reach the image
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ipynb_checkpoints
**/.venv
**/venv

# Run output. Nothing here is an input, and outputs/ in particular can be gigabytes of
# checkpoints that would be copied into the context on every build.
outputs
outputs_*
cache
**/*.pt
**/*.pth
**/*.ckpt
**/*.npz

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# data/README.md is deliberately NOT excluded: it is the provenance record for the vendored
# corpus and travels with the data it describes.
